{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["The reason for <b>all the words of YHWH that He had sent him</b>: that he told him all the matters that had passed between him and the Holy One, blessed be He, and all that he had been refusing the mission, and that he was sent against his will. And this is the meaning of <b>all</b>. And in the Midrash Ḥazita (Shir HaShirim Rabbah 4:12), the Rabbis said that he revealed to him the Explicit Name. They would interpret it as meaning that he told him the Names mentioned above in which He had sent him, and the Name that emerges from them, and he explained them to them."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "הב\"ה resolved as הקב\"ה, 'the Holy One, blessed be He.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:18.528264909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}